{"name":"Bachelor Button","hex":"#4abbd5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bachelor","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person, especially a man, who is socially regarded as able to marry but has not yet.","A bachelor apartment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bachelor"},{"term":"button","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knob or disc that is passed through a loop or (buttonhole), serving as a fastener. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A mechanical device designed to be pressed with a finger in order to open or close an electric circuit or to activate a mechanism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten with a button.","To be fastened by a button or buttons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/button"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bachelor button (sewing)","blocks":[{"text":"A bachelor button is a button that can be attached without sewing. It uses a stud pressed through fabric and into a top button. They were sold in notion stores in the late 1800s and early 1900s as an emergency repair button. They could be attached and removed. The poem “A Bachelor's Button” is a lament by a man whose lover never sewed his button on his coat and had to use a bachelor's button to repair it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Bachelorbutton.jpg/330px-Bachelorbutton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bachelor_button_(sewing)","wikidata":"Q25222470"},{"title":"Bachelor's buttons","blocks":[{"text":"Bachelor's buttons is a common name for several plant species bearing buttonlike heads of composite flowers"},{"items":["Gomphrena canescens, native to Australia.","Gomphrena globosa, native to Brazil, Panama and Guatemala.","Centaurea cyanus, native to Europe, including the British Isles and cultivated as an annual ornamental plant.","Centaurea montana, native to Europe, excluding the British Isles, and cultivated as a perennial ornamental plant.","Kerria japonica 'Pleniflora', a double-flowered cultivar of a species native to China, Japan and Korea.","Ranunculus aconitifolius, native to central Europe."]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bachelor's_buttons","wikidata":"Q16479674"},{"title":"Bachelor","blocks":[{"text":"A bachelor is a man who is not and has never been married."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bachelor","wikidata":"Q516445"},{"title":"Button","blocks":[{"text":"A button is a fastener that joins two pieces of fabric together by slipping through a loop or by sliding through a buttonhole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Reserveknapper_til_Hans%27_uniform.jpg/330px-Reserveknapper_til_Hans%27_uniform.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Button","wikidata":"Q160464"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Three_holes_buttons.jpg/500px-Three_holes_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Three_holes_buttons.jpg/1280px-Three_holes_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Three_holes_buttons.jpg/500px-Three_holes_buttons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern buttons made from vegetable ivory","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_holes_buttons.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Spanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg/500px-Spanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Spanish_button_ca._1650-75_12mm_f%26b.jpg/500px-Spanish_button_ca._1650